#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063973 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064237 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "53bf0d67-be51-5194-884b-e275d58a2ba1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection of Two Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "f55392b5-8cb5-516c-8151-051768d813dd" :question/math-academy-id "e-13948" :question/problem "Find the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x - 5 \\leq 1$ and $7x +11 < -3$." :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- We start by solving $2x - 5 \\leq 1$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2x - 5 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x - 5 + 5 & \\le 1 + 5 \\\\ 2x & \\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ x & \\le 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/60/600e2c9a8560e61697b480de35a3d077d13624ba616514a060c4bcf4fa3f47e4.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7x +11 < -3$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}7x + 11 & < - 3 \\\\ 7x + 11 - 11 & < - 3 - 11 \\\\ 7x & < - 14 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & < \\frac{-14}{7} \\\\ x & < - 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/b6/b6014786331de7693c3a1e0d502ea79fb049252fe9f3ecfcd49a873d996896fe.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/2e/2e5425630ece3ab7006378a7930aae0452c3d5261e7bfb579c97daf572b71d22.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x < -2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064238 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "79f6f04e-ecce-5318-b72b-46478661ced0" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Systems of Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "f088ca30-8538-57e7-9882-99d5c155c505" :question/math-academy-id "e-13952" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n${5x - 35 \\ge 0; 7x > 21$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both\n\n$$\n5x-35 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nand $7x > 21$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $5x-35 \\geq 0$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}5x - 35 & \\ge 0 \\\\ 5x - 35 + 35 & \\ge 0 + 35 \\\\ 5x & \\ge 35 \\\\ \\frac{5x}{5} & \\ge \\frac{35}{5} \\\\ x & \\ge 7\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/48/4875553156dc3e4ec15ecdb6c848fd43d519941123d0d9763d209e9f1d6a52f6.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7x > 21$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}7x & > 21 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & > \\frac{21}{7} \\\\ x & > 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/f7/f7a68da2d31f0bfe038252ac0dc9151d81bf854a7d33da591cbaef05f52bda28.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/27/27fbd7222a4a02d4a14c17c4043b55a2828e66c2d4dcb019598ea5efef2089e6.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is\n\n$$\nx \\geq 7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063978 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c9460289-3e48-558e-b149-3e12a25e50a6" :knowledge-point/title "Flipping the Sign of an Inequality in a System"}] :question/id #uuid "0a39d86b-ab9b-5479-9d7b-726247558397" :question/math-academy-id "e-13959" :question/problem "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n${2 - 7x \\ge 2; 10x - 3 \\ge 7$" :question/worked-solution "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $x$ that satisfy both\n\n$$\n2-7x \\geq 2\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n10x-3 \\geq 7\n$$\n\nsimultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $2-7x \\geq 2$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 - 7x & \\ge 2 \\\\ 2 - 7x - 2 & \\ge 2 - 2 \\\\ -7x & \\ge 0 \\\\ (-1) \\cdot (-7x) & \\le (-1) \\cdot 0 \\\\ 7x & \\le 0 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & \\le \\frac{0}{7} \\\\ x & \\le 0\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/96/96957d6e6c105fd3734dbe478850287c1c8771873b94fedc4ee0ed5cebf41c40.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $10x-3 \\geq 7$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}10x - 3 & \\ge 7 \\\\ 10x - 3 + 3 & \\ge 7 + 3 \\\\ 10x & \\ge 10 \\\\ \\frac{10x}{10} & \\ge \\frac{10}{10} \\\\ x & \\ge 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/9d/9d2d2e7b05bd4bcaf964353266e35bb12f406372ade7255accf6dc3503046f5c.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/98/98654d9ff727e680d0e1ba1ff88b9202248aba6a75a5002a01cd9d628cb6c5b3.png)\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, no values of $x$ satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063979 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/id #uuid "d2726a15-72d6-5c0c-8302-68ba55f8734d" :question/math-academy-id "e-13961" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $1 \\lt 3x-2 \\leq 7$ and $2-3x \\leq -4$." :question/worked-solution "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $1 \\lt 3x-2 \\leq 7 \\,$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & < 3x - 2 \\le 7 \\\\ 1 + 2 & < 3x - 2 + 2 \\le 7 + 2 \\\\ 3 & < 3x \\le 9 \\\\ \\frac{3}{3} & < \\frac{3x}{3} \\le \\frac{9}{3} \\\\ 1 & < x \\le 3\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/34/341633f5e132e1ab07af8969161c20443d65aec7e89ce0bc600868504dd19f9b.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2-3x \\leq -4 \\,$:\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 - 3x & \\le - 4 \\\\ 2 - 3x - 2 & \\le - 4 - 2 \\\\ -3x & \\le - 6 \\\\ (-1) \\cdot (-3x) & \\ge (-1) \\cdot (-6) \\\\ 3x & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & \\ge \\frac{6}{3} \\\\ x & \\ge 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](images/06/06dafae801f6ed3900474c72437eb5a40376ed06bebf3c6eb568e6237c2d930d.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/9b/9b3bd118d0940d6336a32c25b8556dccb3c4085f75da7d3d8628725cf9105071.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x \\in [2,3]$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064240 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d3286dfe-5140-5ba7-8e34-c98e63dc15c0" :knowledge-point/title "Systems Containing Compound Inequalities"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "f220bdb6-94ea-5c8c-8b3e-c792109f5378" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061710} {:answer-field/id #uuid "111a1feb-4973-5295-afcc-add4bd2c219c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061711} {:answer-field/id #uuid "53ba2e9b-e8b7-54b0-aab1-e28c9a2494cc" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061712}] :question/id #uuid "5b65ad66-5f52-5406-9e2e-007075702256" :question/math-academy-id "q-220299" :question/problem "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $-1 \\le 2 - x \\le 3$ and $2x + 1 \\ge 5$. {{field-1}}\n$\\le x$\n{{field-2}} {{field-3}}"}]}
